      <span class="section-kicker">How it works</span>
      <h2>Certification path building over a federated graph of CAs.</h2>
      <p>
        PolarisChain does not replace PKIX validation. It provides a formal layer for
        modelling federation relationships, discovering viable routes, and selecting an
        optimal path between the issuer side of a certificate request and governed trust
        points across multidomain PKI environments.
      </p>
